---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
const site = 'https://ewo.cam';
const slug = 'about';
---

<Base
  title="About EWO — Webcam Model & Studio Promotion Agency"
  description="EWO is a digital marketing agency specializing in audience growth for webcam models and studios across 13 countries. Legitimate strategies, real results."
  lang="en"
  hreflang={[
    { lang: 'en', url: `${site}/about` },
    { lang: 'de', url: `${site}/de/about` },
    { lang: 'es', url: `${site}/es/about` },
    { lang: 'ro', url: `${site}/ro/about` },
    { lang: 'uk', url: `${site}/uk/about` },
    { lang: 'ru', url: `${site}/ru/about` },
  ]}
>
  <article class="page-content">
    <div class="container">

      <header class="page-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>EWO — Webcam Model and Studio Promotion Agency</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          EWO is a digital marketing agency built specifically for the live streaming industry.
          We provide audience growth services for webcam models and studios across North America,
          Western Europe, and Eastern Europe — with strategies built around how this industry
          actually works, not generic marketing advice.
        </p>
        <p>We run promotion for models and studios on Chaturbate, Stripchat, and other major platforms — turning traffic into loyal viewers and paying members.</p>
      </header>

      <figure class="page-hero-image">
        <img src="/images/about-ewo-webcam-promotion-agency.svg" alt="About EWO webcam model and studio promotion agency, global team across countries" width="640" height="360" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>


      <section>
        <h2>What We Do</h2>
        <p>
          We help webcam models and studios grow their audiences through legitimate digital marketing:
          platform optimization, streaming schedule strategy, social media presence, and SEO.
          Everything we do is designed to build real, loyal audiences — not inflate vanity metrics.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our clients range from independent models who are just starting out and need their first
          consistent audience, to established multi-model studios looking to scale traffic across
          their entire roster.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Our Services</h2>

        <h3>For Models</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/model-promotion">Model Promotion</a> — profile optimization, schedule strategy, social media growth</li>
          <li><a href="/new-model-growth">New Model Growth Program</a> — structured 30-day program for models starting from zero</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>For Studios</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/studio-traffic">Studio Traffic Growth</a> — multi-model scheduling, regional targeting, studio SEO</li>
          <li><a href="/studio-scaling">Studio Scaling</a> — systems and strategy for growing your roster without losing traffic quality</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Educational Resources</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/why-low-viewers-webcam">Why Your Room Has Low Viewers</a></li>
          <li><a href="/how-cam-algorithm-ranks-rooms">How Cam Platform Algorithms Work</a></li>
          <li><a href="/best-streaming-times-by-region">Best Streaming Times by Region</a></li>
          <li><a href="/webcam-model-income-guide">Webcam Model Income Guide</a></li>
          <li><a href="/platforms-we-work-with">Platforms We Work With</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Our Approach</h2>
        <p>
          The webcam industry has no shortage of services offering shortcuts: fake viewers, bot traffic,
          engagement manipulation. We don't offer any of these — not because we're naive about what
          clients sometimes want, but because they consistently destroy accounts, waste money, and
          produce no durable results.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every strategy we recommend is built on the same principle: help you attract viewers who
          genuinely want to watch you, and give them reasons to return. This is slower than buying
          fake traffic. It is also the only thing that actually works over time.
        </p>

        <h3>No Platform Brand Conflicts</h3>
        <p>
          We work across all major live streaming platforms without creating conflicts with platform
          terms of service. Our strategies are built around platform algorithms and audience behavior —
          not workarounds that risk your account standing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Regions We Serve</h2>
        <p>
          We operate across 13 countries and have specific expertise in the traffic dynamics of each market.
          Our geo-specific promotion strategies are built around real regional differences — not just
          translated versions of the same playbook.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/model-promotion-usa">United States</a> — largest market, highest average viewer spend</li>
          <li><a href="/model-promotion-germany">Germany</a> — high-loyalty DACH audience, strong long-term retention</li>
          <li><a href="/model-promotion-romania">Romania</a> — high model supply market, Western audience targeting</li>
          <li><a href="/model-promotion-ukraine">Ukraine</a> — European prime time advantage, international audience focus</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Additional regions: Canada, Colombia, Bulgaria, Russia, Sweden, Poland, France, England, Netherlands.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Who We Work With</h2>
        <p>We serve two distinct audiences with very different needs:</p>

        <h3>Independent Webcam Models</h3>
        <p>
          Models who stream on their own and want professional marketing support to grow their audience,
          increase income, and build a more consistent viewer base — without managing the marketing
          strategy themselves.
        </p>

        <h3>Webcam Studios and Agencies</h3>
        <p>
          Multi-model operations that need scalable traffic systems, coordinated scheduling across
          their roster, and strategies for expanding into new regional markets without losing
          traffic quality.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="cta-section" id="contact">
        <h2>Get Started</h2>
        <p>
          Tell us your situation — model or studio, platforms you work with, and what you're
          trying to achieve. We'll review it and come back with a realistic plan.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/contact">Contact us →</a></p>
      </section>

      <section class="related-articles">
        <h2>Related Articles</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/model-promotion">Model Promotion Services</a></li>
          <li><a href="/studio-traffic">Studio Traffic</a></li>
          <li><a href="/why-low-viewers-webcam">Why Your Webcam Room Has Low Viewers</a></li>
          <li><a href="/how-cam-algorithm-ranks-rooms">How the Cam Algorithm Ranks Rooms</a></li>
          <li><a href="/platforms-we-work-with">Platforms We Work With</a></li>
          <li><a href="/contact">Contact Us</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-content { padding-block: 3rem 5rem; }
  .page-header { margin-bottom: 3rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding-bottom: 2rem; }
  .eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: .75rem; }
  .page-header h1 { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.125rem; max-width: 60ch; }
  article section { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  article h2 { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  article h3 { margin-bottom: .5rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  article p { margin-bottom: .875rem; }
  article ul { margin: .75rem 0 .875rem 1.5rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .5rem; }
  article li { color: var(--fg-muted); }
  article a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  article a:hover { color: var(--accent-hover); }
  .cta-section { background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 2rem; margin-top: 3rem; }
</style>
